WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.033
Hi, readers!

2
00:00:02.063 --> 00:00:06.393
Today we're reading a story called The
Missing Library Book.

3
00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.511
As we read, we'll look for the plot.

4
00:00:09.541 --> 00:00:14.477
That's what happens first, the problem,
and how the problem gets solved.

5
00:00:16.177 --> 00:00:18.688
Have you ever lost something you needed?

6
00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:21.039
Maybe a shoe, or your homework?

7
00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:23.452
Think about how that felt.

8
00:00:26.032 --> 00:00:30.731
In this story, a girl named Rosa loses
something important.

9
00:00:30.761 --> 00:00:32.742
Let's find out what happens.

10
00:00:34.442 --> 00:00:38.867
On Monday, Rosa checked out a book about
sea turtles.

11
00:00:39.147 --> 00:00:43.879
It had bright pictures of baby turtles
racing to the ocean.

12
00:00:44.159 --> 00:00:46.887
She read it every night that week.

13
00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:51.212
On Friday, the book was due back at the
library.

14
00:00:52.042 --> 00:00:55.675
Friday morning, Rosa looked in her
backpack.

15
00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.896
The book was not there.

16
00:00:58.176 --> 00:01:01.692
She checked under her bed and behind the
couch.

17
00:01:01.972 --> 00:01:03.990
Her heart beat fast.

18
00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:08.487
She did not want to tell the librarian
that she had lost it.

19
00:01:09.317 --> 00:01:11.900
Rosa sat down and thought hard.

20
00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.574
Where had she read the book last?

21
00:01:14.854 --> 00:01:21.237
She remembered reading on the porch swing
after dinner, so she ran outside to look.

22
00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:25.603
There was the book, tucked between two
cushions.

23
00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:30.517
The cover was a little damp from the
morning dew, but it was fine.

24
00:01:30.797 --> 00:01:33.981
Rosa let out a long, happy breath.

25
00:01:34.261 --> 00:01:38.358
Rosa dried it with a towel and put it in
her backpack.

26
00:01:39.188 --> 00:01:42.877
At school, she told the librarian what had
happened.

27
00:01:43.157 --> 00:01:48.623
The librarian smiled and said that
thinking back was a smart plan.

28
00:01:48.903 --> 00:01:51.899
Rosa checked out a new book that day.

29
00:01:53.849 --> 00:01:56.238
Let me show you how I find the plot.

30
00:01:56.268 --> 00:01:59.418
First, I look for what happens at the
beginning.

31
00:01:59.998 --> 00:02:03.856
On Monday, Rosa checked out a book about
sea turtles.

32
00:02:03.886 --> 00:02:05.974
This is the first event.

33
00:02:06.004 --> 00:02:07.722
It starts the story.

34
00:02:08.302 --> 00:02:10.539
Next, I look for the problem.

35
00:02:10.569 --> 00:02:11.765
Here it is.

36
00:02:11.795 --> 00:02:13.666
The book was not there.

37
00:02:13.696 --> 00:02:16.043
This is where the problem starts.

38
00:02:16.623 --> 00:02:18.112
Why does it matter?

39
00:02:18.142 --> 00:02:21.901
She did not want to tell the librarian
that she had lost it.

40
00:02:21.931 --> 00:02:23.577
Rosa is worried.

41
00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:27.380
Now let's try one together.

42
00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.731
Find the sentence where the problem gets
solved.

43
00:02:30.761 --> 00:02:32.649
Look at paragraph four.

44
00:02:38.229 --> 00:02:39.667
Did you find it?

45
00:02:39.697 --> 00:02:42.832
There was the book, tucked between two
cushions.

46
00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.716
Rosa finds her book.

47
00:02:44.746 --> 00:02:46.515
The problem is solved!

48
00:02:47.095 --> 00:02:50.916
And at the end, she told the librarian
what had happened.

49
00:02:52.616 --> 00:02:53.996
Now you try.

50
00:02:54.026 --> 00:02:56.263
Where does Rosa find the book?

51
00:02:56.293 --> 00:02:58.232
Is it A, under her bed?

52
00:02:58.262 --> 00:02:59.972
B, in her backpack?

53
00:03:00.002 --> 00:03:01.825
C, on the porch swing?

54
00:03:01.855 --> 00:03:03.918
Or D, at the library?

55
00:03:09.498 --> 00:03:11.123
The answer is C.

56
00:03:11.153 --> 00:03:16.154
Rosa finds the book on the porch swing,
tucked between two cushions.

57
00:03:16.184 --> 00:03:19.615
She found it by thinking back to where she
read it last.

58
00:03:21.315 --> 00:03:22.975
Great work today!

59
00:03:23.005 --> 00:03:27.452
A plot has a beginning, a problem, a
solution, and an end.

60
00:03:28.032 --> 00:03:30.037
Rosa checked out a book.

61
00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.739
The book went missing.

62
00:03:31.769 --> 00:03:33.828
She thought back and found it.

63
00:03:33.858 --> 00:03:35.998
Then she told the librarian.

64
00:03:36.578 --> 00:03:41.579
Next time you read a story, look for the
problem, and how it gets solved.
